  "why_these_measures": "Rank agreement says whether the model orders the space; top-k stability says whether its recommendation survives being refitted, which average precision hides; distance to the measured front is the quantity the search paper cares about, and a model can rank well while placing the front wrongly. They saturate at different sizes and the largest is the answer."
